            <title>0.6.7</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 09:49:39 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>135</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.6.7</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[- Settings > Pi Runtime has a new Engine picker. PiG (Pi in Go, a native port of Pi) can run Pi tasks instead of Pi. It uses your ~/.pi/agent setup, so sessions, extensions and logins carry over. A switch applies to the next session; running sessions keep their engine.
- Subagent extensions such as pi-open-agents work under PiG through a small compatibility file PiBoard adds to the PiG extension cache, until PiG fixes this upstream (MichaelKinsy/PiG#395).
- Settings: OpenCode, Claude Code and PiG can be set up from Settings when they are missing. After a confirmation, the official setup script runs in a terminal sheet. Update runs opencode upgrade, claude update or pig update the same way.
- Quitting while a setup or update is running now asks first.
]]></description>
